## Context

Audit 0127 drift A: the spec header table (row for Tag) hardcodes the
values `needs-human, deferred`. The code defers to `.ergrc [tags]` via
`effectiveTagSet`, falling back to `defaultTags` when no `.ergrc` exists.
The manual already documents the `.ergrc` override. The spec does not.

## Actions

- In `tickets/spec-erg-v1.md`, header table row for `Tag`, update the
  Values column to note that the vocabulary is configurable via
  `.ergrc [tags]`, with the listed values as defaults.
- Add a sentence after the header table or in the Tag description
  explaining the override mechanism.

## Exit criteria

- Spec header table mentions `.ergrc [tags]` configurability.
- `make test` passes (no code changes).
